    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 297,
        "text": "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to the community garden meeting. I know it's a busy time, so let's start. First, the good news: we've received a small grant from the city to buy new tools and seeds. (1) Because the grant is only for one year, we need to decide how to spend it wisely. Any ideas?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "6edea8e6c8f882993c5768eee06614904d961f3b97a792350b7d05d4b021f226",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 302,
        "sourceEnd": 485,
        "text": "Yes, I think we should buy a shed to store the tools. (2) If we don't have a shed, the tools will get rusty in the rain. Also, a shed can be used for meetings when the weather is bad.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "a170f6eb27b758e58a1f82e431936f04557cdfecc9fdd906e897a17fcadd4a59",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 490,
        "sourceEnd": 627,
        "text": "That's a good point. But a shed might be expensive. (3) We may not have enough money for both a shed and new seeds. What do others think?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "143821676414ccce1a26413af88b65f42aefc6ffb02e1c8de01b902b24ecc71e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 629,
        "sourceEnd": 862,
        "text": "W2: I agree with the shed idea, but maybe we can build it ourselves to save money. (4) Although none of us are professional builders, we can watch online videos and learn. My neighbour built his own shed last year, and it looks fine.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "af12951db3e834371f346a8fb2d50730786849dd166a570a17987407aed722a5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 867,
        "sourceEnd": 1062,
        "text": "OK, so we could build a shed. But we also need to think about the seeds. (5) Since we want to grow vegetables for the food bank, we should buy seeds that are easy to grow, like beans and carrots.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "31b7ddb66164aeeafd0c97faa8bbf3d98ee978b0c8a605d456cf8d649912389a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1067,
        "sourceEnd": 1206,
        "text": "Right. And (6) even though beans are cheap, they need support to climb, so we might need to buy sticks or nets. That could add to the cost.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "ea61dc38721415a25f9031821feaf1016f6381937ba5c38c782a5f50f87bde09",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1211,
        "sourceEnd": 1404,
        "text": "True. Let's not forget the water problem. (7) The tap is far from the garden, so we have to carry water in buckets. That's hard work for older members. Could we use some money for a water tank?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "0ef5e4f965cc028baa20ce05f4a186e3e578518b9c436d2f60a0907ad5c9a740",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 1406,
        "sourceEnd": 1572,
        "text": "W2: A water tank would be great, but (8) unless we get permission from the council, we can't put a large tank there. The council might say no because of safety rules.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "2b8c197aa402c414a8c68710ee5a0607beb2adb1f3acc0382b233f282e54724c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1577,
        "sourceEnd": 1774,
        "text": "Hmm. So we have three possible things: a shed, seeds, and a water tank. (9) We can't afford all three, so we need to prioritise. Let's vote next week. But before that, does anyone have other ideas?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "8544a3c594e2bb2cbab5e9a0e787fd582317a642cd8ccd8ca708a761ea0d8188",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1779,
        "sourceEnd": 1966,
        "text": "What about asking local businesses for donations? (10) If we explain our plan clearly, they might give us materials for free. For example, a hardware store could donate wood for the shed.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "e58c95d302a6ad950ff93cf64a2d55e5d492d697cf66a20defc680ceb843b4b5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1971,
        "sourceEnd": 2151,
        "text": "That's a clever idea. OK, so let's summarise: we'll ask for donations, and then decide between the shed, seeds, and water tank. Thanks for your time. Let's meet again next Tuesday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "a08028de2171ec3ef5f6e58ed8635484b56c810e357fe29c0eefce31f84b6352",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
